  "query_preview": "..\n\nThe rest of today through Tuesday...\n\nUnseasonably warm, dry, and breezy conditions continue into\nThursday, bringing elevated to critical fire weather conditions.\nThursday is expected to be warmer, drier, and a little breezier\nthan today, with highs in the 80s to near 90, relative humidity in\nthe low teens percent, and wind gusts of 30 to 40 mph over the\nfoothills west of Billings and gusts of 25 to 35 mph near the\nDakota border. Across the rest of the area, gusts of 15 to 25 mph\nwill be common. A Red Flag Warning is in effect Thursday for \nportions of the region west and north of Billings and over far \nsoutheastern Montana into the Dakotas. Take care not to cause a\nspark!\n\nA cold front will move through late Thursday/early Friday \nmorning, shifting winds to the northeast and beginning a trend\ntowards cooler weather. Highs will be in the upper 60s to upper \n70s Friday, falling to upper 50s over the northwest to low 70s\nover the southeast for the weekend as a trough approaches and\nmoves through. Friday into Saturday, ahead of the trough, weak \nshortwaves will bring isolated to scattered (20-60% chance, \nhighest over the mountains) showers and weak thunderstorms.\n\nModels are in better agreement for the system this weekend into\nearly next week. There will be a better chance (50-80%) for\nwidespread showers late Saturday into late Sunday/early Monday.\nCurrently, the best chance for 0.5\" of precipitation (40-70%) with\nthis system is from Billings west and north. With the cooling\ntemperatures, snow levels fall to 7,500 ft late Sunday night/early\nMonday morning. A few inches of snow may fall above 9,000 ft (30%\nchance) with locally higher amounts over the highest peaks. Those\nwith recreation plans in the high country should prepare for\nwintry conditions! \n\nOvernight temperatures are forecast to drop into the mid 30s and\n40s Friday night through Sunday night. All foothills locations \ncurrently have a 40 to 60% chance of a frost (36 F) Monday \nmorning, while the plains have a 15 to 40% chance. Over the \nfoothills, there is also a low chance (10-30%) for a freeze (32 F)\nMonday morning.\n\nMonday into Tuesday, the system exits the region, bringing dry\nconditions late Monday through Tuesday and allowing highs to\napproach seasonable (70s) Tuesday. Archer",
